{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s -Donn\u00e9es sur la tarification", "keywords": "inland water resources,municipal water treatment,municipal wastewater treatment,water supply reservoirs", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "bf6f186b-3a13-4038-a829-f762c94d2765", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Donn\u00e9es de l'Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey -Pricing Data", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "L'Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s (EEPEU) fait suite \u00e0 l'Enqu\u00eate sur la tarification et l'utilisation de l'eau par les municipalit\u00e9s, qu'a men\u00e9e Environnement Canada tous les deux ou trois ans depuis le d\u00e9but des ann\u00e9es 1980. Cet ensemble de donn\u00e9es contient les r\u00e9sultats de l'enqu\u00eate concernant la tarification de l'eau potable et des eaux us\u00e9es \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle des municipalit\u00e9s.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/eau-water/default.asp?lang=En&n=ED0E12D7-1#pricingdata", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2010-09-28", "time_period_coverage_start": "1991-01-01", "data_series_name": "Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey Data", "url_fra": "", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "2004-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/eau-water/default.asp?lang=EN&n=ED7C2D33-1", "notes": "The Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey (MWWS) is an expansion of the Municipal Water Use and Pricing Survey (MUD), which had been conducted by Environment Canada every two or three years since the early 1980s. This dataset contains the results of the survey regarding water and wastewater pricing at the municipal level.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "ressources hydriques int\u00e9rieures,traitement des eaux municipales,traitement des eaux us\u00e9es municipales,r\u00e9servoirs d'alimentation en eau"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s - Donn\u00e9es sur l'utilisation de l'eau", "keywords": "dataset,tabular,inland water resources,stream discharge,water supply reservoirs,municipal water treatment,municipal wastewater treatment", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "c279da5d-62f0-4942-bfc5-0a5b74f8df65", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Don\u00e9es de l'Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey - Water Use Data", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "L'Enqu\u00eate sur l'eau potable et les eaux us\u00e9es des municipalit\u00e9s (EEPEU) fait suite \u00e0 l'Enqu\u00eate sur la tarification et l'utilisation de l'eau par les municipalit\u00e9s, qu'a men\u00e9e Environnement Canada tous les deux ou trois ans depuis le d\u00e9but des ann\u00e9es 1980. Cet ensemble de donn\u00e9es contient les r\u00e9sultats de l'enqu\u00eate concernant l'utilisation de l'eau et de l'eau potable et des eaux us\u00e9es \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle des municipalit\u00e9s. Ces donn\u00e9es peuvent \u00eatre utilis\u00e9es pour \u00e9valuer les tendances qui permettraient de faire une utilisation plus avis\u00e9e des ressources hydriques.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/eau-water/default.asp?lang=En&n=ED0E12D7-1#wateruse", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2010-09-27", "time_period_coverage_start": "1983-01-01", "data_series_name": "Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey Data", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/eau-water/default.asp?lang=FR&n=ED7C2D33-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "2006-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "2011-01-19", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/eau-water/default.asp?lang=EN&n=ED7C2D33-1 ", "notes": "The Municipal Water and Wastewater Survey (MWWS) is an expansion of the Municipal Water Use and Pricing Survey (MUD), which had been conducted by Environment Canada every two or three years since the early 1980s. This dataset contains the results of the survey regarding water and waste water use at the municipal level. This data can be used to see trends that can lead to wiser use of water resources.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "ensemble de donn\u00e9es,tabulaire,ressources hydriques int\u00e9rieures,d\u00e9bit,r\u00e9servoirs d'alimentation en eau,traitement des eaux municipales,traitement des eaux us\u00e9es municipales"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Magn\u00e9tom\u00e8tres CANOPUS-CARISMA", "keywords": "magnetometer CARISMA CANOPUS", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "06f5e364-6e2c-4d1c-95c2-9fb7d871ca20", "subject": "Science and Technology  Sciences et technologie", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "CARISMA magnetometer network", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le r\u00e9seau de magn\u00e9tom\u00e8tres CARISMA (www.carisma.ca), pr\u00e9c\u00e9demment appell\u00e9 CANOPUS est op\u00e9r\u00e9 par l'Universit\u00e9 de l'Alberta. Les auteurs qui utilisent des donn\u00e9es sont pri\u00e9s de suivre les r\u00e8gles \u00e0 www.carisma.ca/CARISMADataUse.  Pour toute utilisation ou distribution de donn\u00e9es, SVP inclure les r\u00e9f\u00e9rences appropri\u00e9es, telles que: \"Les auteurs remercient I.R. Mann, D.K. Milling et le autres membres de l'\u00e9quipe CARISMA pour leurs donn\u00e9es. CARISMA est op\u00e9r\u00e9 par l' Universi\u00e9y de l'Alberta, avec le support de l'agence spatiale Canadienne.\" SVP aussi inclure cette r\u00e9f\u00e9rence \u00e0 CARISMA: Mann, I. R., et al. (2008), The upgraded CARISMA magnetometer array in the THEMIS era, Space Sci. Rev., 141, 413-451, doi:10.1007/s11214-008-9457-6.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "other", "url": "ftp://ftp.asc-csa.gc.ca/users/OpenData_DonneesOuvertes/pub/carisma/", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-04-05", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "", "url_fra": "", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "", "notes": "The CARISMA (www.carisma.ca), previously known as CANOPUS, magnetometer network is operated by the University of Alberta. Users of the data are asked to follow the rules of the road at www.carisma.ca/CARISMADataUse. Any use or distribution of the data please include an appropriate acknowledgement, such as: \"The authors thank I.R. Mann, D.K. Milling and the rest of the CARISMA team for data. CARISMA is operated by the University of Alberta, funded by the Canadian Space Agency.\" The following CARISMA reference paper should also be cited: Mann, I. R., et al. (2008), The upgraded CARISMA magnetometer array in the THEMIS era, Space Sci. Rev., 141, 413-451, doi:10.1007/s11214-008-9457-6. ", "owner_org": "csa-asc", "keywords_fra": "magnetom\u00e8tre CARISMA CANOPUS"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "L'empreinte des perturbations anthropiques sur les aires de r\u00e9partition du caribou bor\u00e9al au Canada - Telle qu'interpr\u00e9t\u00e9e \u00e0 partir d'imagerie satellitaire Landsat de 2008 \u00e0 2010 (Cr\u00e9\u00e9s avec les aires  de r\u00e9partition mise \u00e0 jour 2012)", "keywords": "anthropogeneic disturbance,boreal,forest,caribou,habitat,mapping,landcover,landuse", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "f34dcb32-4845-4e88-b125-5ac03c6e4a7f", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "L'empreinte des perturbations anthropiques sur les aires de r\u00e9partition du caribou bor\u00e9al au Canada  (Cr\u00e9\u00e9s avec les aires  de r\u00e9partition mise \u00e0 jour 2012)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Anthropogenic disturbance footprint within boreal caribou ranges across Canada - As interpreted from 2008-2010 Landsat satellite imagery (Updated to 2012 range boundaries)", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Dans le cadre d'une \u00e9valuation scientifique de l'habitat essentiel du caribou bor\u00e9al (Environnement Canada, 2011, se reporter \u00e0 la r\u00e9f\u00e9rence compl\u00e8te dans la documentation fournie), la Division des sciences et de la technologie du paysage d'Environnement Canada a \u00e9t\u00e9 charg\u00e9e de r\u00e9aliser une cartographie d\u00e9taill\u00e9e des perturbations anthropiques dans l'ensemble des aires de r\u00e9partition connues du caribou. Ces donn\u00e9es ont permis aux chercheurs de mieux comprendre les caract\u00e9ristiques qui influent sur la p\u00e9rennit\u00e9 des populations de caribou. Le processus de cartographie a \u00e9t\u00e9 \u00e9tabli pour constituer, selon une m\u00e9thodologie commune, un ensemble de donn\u00e9es g\u00e9ospatiales coh\u00e9rent, fiable et reproductible \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale. Les m\u00e9thodes \u00e9labor\u00e9es ont privil\u00e9gi\u00e9 la cartographie des perturbations \u00e0 un moment particulier et n'ont pas \u00e9t\u00e9 con\u00e7ues pour d\u00e9terminer l'\u00e2ge des perturbations. Cette derni\u00e8re information pourrait toutefois pr\u00e9senter de l'int\u00e9r\u00eat en ce qui concerne les perturbations jug\u00e9es non permanentes comme, par exemple, les blocs de coupe. Les ensembles de donn\u00e9es obtenus ont \u00e9t\u00e9 utilis\u00e9s pour la mod\u00e9lisation des fonctions de s\u00e9lection des ressources et de l'habitat et pour \u00e9valuer les niveaux de perturbation d'ensemble pour chacune des aires de r\u00e9partition du caribou. Les perturbations anthropiques de 57 aires de r\u00e9partition du caribou dans l'ensemble du Canada ont \u00e9t\u00e9 cartographi\u00e9es. Ces aires de r\u00e9partition \u00e9taient d\u00e9limit\u00e9es par province et territoire dans l'ensemble du pays. Les perturbations ont \u00e9t\u00e9 cartographi\u00e9es dans ces aires de r\u00e9partition en utilisant l'imagerie satellitaire Landsat-5 de 2008 \u00e0 2010 pour que le jeu de donn\u00e9es soit le plus \u00e0 jour possible. Certaines zones ont d'abord \u00e9t\u00e9 cartographi\u00e9es selon qu'elles correspondaient aux dates des donn\u00e9es d\u00e9mographiques sur le caribou d\u00e9j\u00e0 recueillies; des images plus r\u00e9centes ont cependant \u00e9t\u00e9 utilis\u00e9es et des entit\u00e9s de perturbations suppl\u00e9mentaires ayant \u00e9t\u00e9 observ\u00e9es depuis la date de la premi\u00e8re cartographie ont \u00e9t\u00e9 ajout\u00e9es. Dans le contexte du projet, la perturbation anthropique a \u00e9t\u00e9 d\u00e9finie comme \u00e9tant toute perturbation qui a \u00e9t\u00e9 caus\u00e9e par l'humain dans le paysage naturel et qui pourrait \u00eatre rep\u00e9r\u00e9e visuellement sur l'imagerie Landsat \u00e0 une \u00e9chelle de 1/50 000. Une unit\u00e9 cartographique minimale de 2 hectares ou d'environ 22 pixels Landsat contigus a \u00e9t\u00e9 choisie. Chaque type d'entit\u00e9 de perturbation a \u00e9t\u00e9 repr\u00e9sent\u00e9 dans la base de donn\u00e9es par une ligne ou un polygone, selon le type de description g\u00e9om\u00e9trique correspondant. Les cat\u00e9gories des entit\u00e9s polygonales \u00e9taient les suivantes : blocs de coupe, mines, r\u00e9servoirs, agglom\u00e9rations, puits, zones agricoles, installations p\u00e9troli\u00e8res et gazi\u00e8res et entit\u00e9s inconnues. Les cat\u00e9gories des entit\u00e9s lin\u00e9aires \u00e9taient les suivantes : routes, lignes de transport d'\u00e9lectricit\u00e9, chemins de fer, lignes sismiques, pipelines, barrages, pistes d'atterrissage et entit\u00e9s inconnues. Une d\u00e9finition claire de chaque type d'\u00e9l\u00e9ment anthropique (se reporter \u00e0 l'annexe 7.2 de l'\u00e9valuation scientifique) a \u00e9t\u00e9 formul\u00e9e de fa\u00e7on \u00e0 ce que l'identification des diverses perturbations pouvant \u00eatre relev\u00e9es sur les images demeure uniforme quelle que soit la personne charg\u00e9e de l'interpr\u00e9tation de l'imagerie. Divers ensembles de donn\u00e9es vectorielles accessoires ont aid\u00e9 \u00e0 d\u00e9tecter, classifier et num\u00e9riser les perturbations sur les images Landsat (un tableau comportant la liste des jeux de donn\u00e9es et de leurs sources est joint en fichier s\u00e9par\u00e9). Des donn\u00e9es accessoires ont aussi \u00e9t\u00e9 utilis\u00e9es pour orienter l'interpr\u00e9tation et la d\u00e9signation des entit\u00e9s. Cependant, parce que l'exhaustivit\u00e9 et l'\u00e9chelle de ces donn\u00e9es accessoires variaient souvent dans l'ensemble du pays, les entit\u00e9s n'ont \u00e9t\u00e9 num\u00e9ris\u00e9es que si elles \u00e9taient visibles sur les images \u00e0 une \u00e9chelle d'affichage de 1/50 000. Un contr\u00f4le de la qualit\u00e9 a \u00e9t\u00e9 effectu\u00e9 par un deuxi\u00e8me interpr\u00e8te afin de s'assurer de la qualit\u00e9, de l'int\u00e9gralit\u00e9 et de la coh\u00e9rence des donn\u00e9es recueillies. Comme il n'\u00e9tait pas possible d'\u00e9valuer l'exactitude des donn\u00e9es, une analyse de l'\u00e9valuation de la qualit\u00e9 a \u00e9t\u00e9 effectu\u00e9e sur des \u00e9chantillons en utilisant des images SPOT \u00e0 haute r\u00e9solution. Les r\u00e9sultats sont inclus dans la documentation fournie. Un tampon de 500m (radial), repr\u00e9sentant la zone d'influence sur les populations de caribou bor\u00e9al, a \u00e9t\u00e9 ajout\u00e9 aux donn\u00e9es vectorielles afin de calculer le niveau de perturbation totale dans chaque aire de r\u00e9partition, et utiliser \u00e9galement pour l'\u00e9valuation int\u00e9gr\u00e9e du risque. Les polygones repr\u00e9sentant les feux ont \u00e9t\u00e9 fusionn\u00e9s \u00e0 l'empreinte anthropique afin de cr\u00e9er une empreinte de perturbation totale.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": " http://data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/8/6/E/86EEA60F-CB81-4F97-9842-97687AC36AE1/Field_Names_and_Descriptions_-_ENGLISH_-_UPDATED_2012.txt|Field_Names_and_Descriptions_-_ENGLISH_-_UPDATED_2012.txt", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/data_donnees/STB-DGST/001/Boreal_Caribou_Anthropogenic_Disturbance_Footprint_Mapping_-_SUMMARY_-_ENGLISH.doc, http://ec.gc.ca/data_donnees/STB-DGST/001/Anthropogeneic_Disturbance_Mapping_Methods_Appendix_-_ENGLISH.pdf", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": " http://data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/C/1/B/C1B515E8-5445-4420-9A3B-F5D543345DA4/Field_Names_and_Descriptions_-_FRENCH_-_UPDATED_2012.txt|Field_Names_and_Descriptions_-_FRENCH_-_UPDATED_2012.txt", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/data_donnees/STB-DGST/001/Boreal_Caribou_Anthropogenic_Disturbance_Footprint_Mapping_-_SUMMARY_-_FRENCH.doc, http://ec.gc.ca/data_donnees/STB-DGST/001/Anthropogeneic_Disturbance_Mapping_Methods_Appendix_-_FRENCH.pdf", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "SHAPE", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/data_donnees/STB-DGST/001/BorealCaribouDisturbanceShapefiles_Updated2012.zip", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2013-01-01", "time_period_coverage_start": "2008-05-01", "data_series_name": "Anthropogenic disturbance footprint within boreal caribou ranges across Canada (Updated 2012)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/faunescience-wildlifescience/default.asp?lang=Fr", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "2010-10-01", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/faunescience-wildlifescience/default.asp?lang=En", "notes": "As part of a scientific assessment of critical habitat for boreal woodland caribou (Environment Canada 2011, see full reference in accompanying documentation), Environment Canada's Landscape Science and Technology Division was tasked with providing detailed anthropogenic disturbance mapping across known caribou ranges. This data allowed researchers to better understand the attributes that have a known effect on caribou population persistence. The mapping process was established to create a nationally consistent, reliable and repeatable geospatial dataset that followed a common methodology. The methods developed were focused on mapping disturbances at a specific point of time, and were not designed to identify the age of disturbances, which can be of particular interest for disturbances that can be considered non-permanent, for example cutblocks. The resultant datasets were used for caribou resource selection function,habitat modeling, and assess overall disturbance levels on each caribou ranges. Anthropogenic disturbances within 57 caribou ranges across Canada were mapped. The ranges were defined by individual Provinces and Territories across Canada. Disturbances were mapped across these ranges using 2008-2010 Landsat-5 satellite imagery to provide the most up to date data possible. Originally some areas were mapped to match the date of collected caribou demographic data, however more recent imagery was used and additional disturbance features that were seen since the original mapping date were added. Within the context of this project, anthropogenic disturbance was defined as any human-caused disturbance to the natural landscape that could be visually identified from Landsat imagery at a viewing scale of 1:50,000. A minimum mapping unit (MMU) of 2 ha or approximately 22 contiguous Landsat pixels was selected. Each disturbance feature type was represented in the database by a line or polygon depending on their geometric description. Polygonal disturbances included: cutblocks, mines, reservoirs, built-up areas, well sites, agriculture, oil and gas facilities, as well as unknown features. Linear disturbances included: roads, railways, powerlines, seismic exploration lines, pipelines, dams, air strips, as well as unknown features. For each anthropogenic feature type, a clear description was established (see Appendix 7.2 of the science assessment) to maintain consistency in identifying the various disturbances in the imagery by the different interpreters. Various ancillary vector datasets were used as aids in detecting, classifying and digitizing disturbances on the Landsat imagery (a table listing these datasets and their sources has been included in a separate file). Ancillary data was used to guide interpretation and feature labelling since the ancillary data was often variable across the country in terms of completeness as well as scale. As a result, features were only digitized if they were visible in the Landsat imagery at a viewing scale of 1:50,000. A 2nd interpreter quality control phase was carried out to ensure high quality, completete and consistent data collection. A quality assessment analysis, since an actual accuracy assessment was not possible, using high resolution SPOT imagery was carried out on a sample basis. Results are included in accompanying documentation. The vector data was buffered by 500m (radius) representing the zone of influence impacting boreal caribou herds in order to calculate range disturbance levels as well as for use in the integrated risk assessment analysis. Fire polygons were merged into the anthropogenic footprint in order to create an overall disturbance footprint.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "perturbation anthropique,for\u00eat,bor\u00e9ale,caribou,habitat,cartographie,couverture terrestre,utilisation des terres"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Divulgation des contrats", "keywords": "Contract,contractor,consultant,information technology,employment,expert advisor,advice,building,installation,service,transport,cleaning,building,office equipment,computer equipment,foreign affairs,international", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "6789e638-b705-41ea-b0ca-430311cd8469", "subject": "Economics and Industry  \u00c9conomie et industrie", "data_series_name_fra": "Divulgation des contrats", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Quarterly | Trimestriel", "title": "Disclosure of contracts", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Cet ensemble de donn\u00e9es concerne les divulgations proactives des contrats de travail au sein des Affaires \u00e9trang\u00e8res et Commerce International. Il y a des informations sur la date de publication, la dur\u00e9e du contrat, la description du contrat, le nom du vendeur ainsi que le montant accord\u00e9 \u00e0 ce contrat. ", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://webcast.international.gc.ca/developer/opendata/spp/contracts_contrats/PD%20FY2012-13_Q1%20-%20To nb%20Post_FINAL-%20OPEN%20DATA.xml", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://webcast.international.gc.ca/developer/opendata/spp/contracts_contrats/PD%20FY2012-13_Q2%20-%20To%20Post_FINAL_OPEN%20DATA.xml", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://webcast.international.gc.ca/developer/opendata/spp/contracts_contrats/PD%20FY2012-13_Q3%20-%20To%20Post_FINAL_OPEN%20DATA.xml", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2011-10-25", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Disclosure of contracts", "url_fra": "http://webcast.international.gc.ca/developer/opendata/spp/contracts_contrats/", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://webcast.international.gc.ca/developer/opendata/spp/contracts_contrats/", "notes": "This dataset relates to disclosures of employment contracts in Foreign Affairs and International Trade. There is information about the date of publication, the term of the contracts, the contracts description, the vendor name, and the cost of these contracts. ", "owner_org": "dfait-maeci", "keywords_fra": "Contrat,contractant,consultant,information,technologie,emploi,expert,conseille,conseill\u00e9,b\u00e2timent,installation,service,transport,nettoyage,\u00e9difice,mat\u00e9riel de bureau,mat\u00e9riel informatique,affaires \u00e9trang\u00e8res,international"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Contrats octroy\u00e9s", "keywords": "standing offers,contracts,contacts,register,new supplier,existing suppliers,calendar,events,businesses,opportunities,seminars,registration,SRI,supply manual,standard acquisitions clauses and conditions,CICP,buyers,procurement,procurement specialists,purchase,goods,services,construction,methods of supply,standing offers,supply arrangements,tenders,ACAN,GSIN,Contract History,awards,procurement business number,Canadian Innovation Commercialization Program,green procurement,Standing Offer Index,SOI,sole source,request for proposal,RFP,request for information,RFI", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "53753f06-8b28-42d7-89f7-04cd014323b0", "subject": "Economics and Industry  \u00c9conomie et industrie", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Weekly | Hebdomadaire", "title": "Contract History", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Les donn\u00e9es sur les Contrats octroy\u00e9s sont des renseignements sur les contrats attribu\u00e9s par Travaux publics et Services gouvernementaux Canada (TPSGC) depuis janvier 2009, au nom des minist\u00e8res et organismes f\u00e9d\u00e9raux.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": " http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/C/0/8/C08CF45B-6BC1-4D07-87D1-57B22B76E1BF/contract-history.txt|contract-history.txt", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": " http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/3/4/8/348C380B-7488-462B-9C7F-