{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Demandes de terres du Haut-Canada (1763-1865) ", "keywords": "Land petitions,Land grants,Ontario,Upper Canada,Genealogy,History,Crown land", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "95adb025-df39-4a74-b2d9-1e5bfb758201", "subject": "History and Archaeology  Histoire et arch\u00e9ologie", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Annually | Annuel", "title": "Upper Canada Land Petitions (1763-1865) ", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "Ontario  Ontario", "notes_fra": "Avant l'arriv\u00e9e des Loyalistes et des colons militaires britanniques, la province actuelle de l'Ontario \u00e9tait un prolongement de la province de Qu\u00e9bec. L'Acte constitutionnel de 1791 divise la colonie de Qu\u00e9bec en deux parties : le Haut-Canada (aujourd'hui l'Ontario) et le Bas-Canada (aujourd'hui le Qu\u00e9bec). Un grand nombre de colons, tant militaires que civils, ont pr\u00e9sent\u00e9 des demandes au gouverneur afin d'obtenir des terres de la Couronne. Les fils et filles de Loyalistes avaient aussi le droit \u00e0 des terres gratuites.\n\nLes Demandes de terres du Haut-Canada contiennent des demandes de concessions ou de baux de terres et d'autres documents administratifs. Cet outil de recherche donne acc\u00e8s \u00e0 plus de 82 000 r\u00e9f\u00e9rences concernant des individus ayant v\u00e9cu dans la province actuelle de l'Ontario entre 1783 et 1865.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/A/0/A/A0AB5A30-4780-447E-BEEA-541040A43A37/001097-txt-e.xml|001097-txt-e.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/8/5/6/8566BB5B-CCB2-4E8A-BDA8-49400C240EB6/001097-txt-f.xml|001097-txt-f.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/900/f11/001097-data.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2010-08-30", "time_period_coverage_start": "1763-01-01", "data_series_name": "", "url_fra": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-f.html", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "1865-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "2012-01-10", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-e.html", "notes": "Before the arrival of the Loyalists and British military settlers, the present-day Province of Ontario was an extension of the Province of Quebec. Following the Constitutional Act of 1791, the colony of Quebec was divided to create Upper Canada (today Ontario) and Lower Canada (today Quebec). Many early settlers, both military and civilian, submitted petitions to the Governor to obtain Crown land. Sons and daughters of Loyalists were also entitled to free lands.\n\nThe Upper Canada Land Petitions contain petitions for grants or leases of land and other administrative records. This research tool provides access to more than 82,000 references to individuals who lived in present-day Ontario between 1783 and 1865.\n", "owner_org": "lac-bac", "keywords_fra": "Demandes de terres,Concessions des terres,Ontario,Haut-Canada,G\u00e9n\u00e9alogie,Histoire,Terres de la Couronne"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Demandes de terres du Bas-Canada  (1626-1865)", "keywords": "Land petitions,Land grants,Qu\u00e9bec,Lower Canada,Genealogy,History,Crown land", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "84de078c-c278-43ca-8217-14f4d2deb835", "subject": "History and Archaeology  Histoire et arch\u00e9ologie", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Annually | Annuel", "title": "Lower Canada Land Petitions (1626-1865) ", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "Quebec  Qu\u00e9bec", "notes_fra": "Les Demandes de terres du Bas-Canada contiennent des p\u00e9titions pour des demandes de concessions ou de baux de terres et d'autres documents administratifs. Cet outil de recherche donne acc\u00e8s \u00e0 plus de 95 000 r\u00e9f\u00e9rences concernant des individus ayant v\u00e9cu dans la province actuelle du Qu\u00e9bec entre 1626 et 1865.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/2/6/7/2679AB5C-59A3-43F6-BF37-075ACC9E510A/001043-txt-e.xml|001043-txt-e.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/6/3/4/634742D9-64A4-40EA-B47A-E9D5FB969485/001043-txt-f.xml|001043-txt-f.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/900/f11/001043-data-prt-1.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/900/f11/001043-data-prt-2.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/900/f11/001043-data-prt-3.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2006-06-20", "time_period_coverage_start": "1626-01-01", "data_series_name": "", "url_fra": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-f.html", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "1865-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "2011-09-08", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-e.html", "notes": "The Lower Canada Land Petitions contain petitions for grants or leases of land and other administrative records. This research tool provides access to more than 95,000 references to individuals who lived in present-day Quebec between  1626 and 1865.", "owner_org": "lac-bac", "keywords_fra": "Demandes de terres,Concessions des terres,Qu\u00e9bec,Bas-Canada,G\u00e9n\u00e9alogie,Histoire,Terres de la Couronne"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Concessions des terres de l'Ouest (1870-1930) ", "keywords": "Land grants,Land petitions,Land patents,Western Canada,Manitoba,Saskatchewan,Alberta,British Columbia,Genealogy,History,Crown land", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "c7affa02-e2c0-42cf-b78f-0dd12eb685d8", "subject": "History and Archaeology  Histoire et arch\u00e9ologie", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Annually | Annuel", "title": "Western Land Grants (1870-1930)", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Cet ensemble de donn\u00e9es  a trait exclusivement aux lettres patentes \u00e9mises par le Bureau des lettres patentes du minist\u00e8re de l'Int\u00e9rieur. Les donn\u00e9es ont \u00e9t\u00e9 extraites des registres des concessions distribu\u00e9es au Manitoba, en Saskatchewan, en Alberta et dans la zone des chemins de fer de la Colombie-Britannique, autour de 1870-1930.\n\nLes lettres patentes contiennent uniquement le nom des concessionnaires, la description de la terre et la date de concession. Elles ne contiennent pas d'autres informations de nature personnelle. Les demandes et dossiers pour les lots de colonisation (homestead), qui sont plus d\u00e9tail\u00e9es, sont conserv\u00e9s dans les d\u00e9p\u00f4ts d'archives provinciales.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/5/9/A/59A84A87-8AF9-4FC5-A8D4-D1032D688489/001007-txt-e.xml|001007-txt-e.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://registry.data.gc.ca/commonwebsol/fileuploads/A/F/1/AF1AC585-2675-4B9D-99A0-64390C1A4AA1/001007-txt-f.xml|001007-txt-f.xml", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/900/f11/001007-data.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2006-06-20", "time_period_coverage_start": "1870-01-01", "data_series_name": "", "url_fra": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-f.html", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "1930-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "2011-09-08", "url": "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/022/022-203-e.htm", "notes": "This dataset relates exclusively to Letters Patent issued by the Lands Patent Branch of the Department of the Interior. The records refer to grants issued in Manitoba, Saskatchewan, Alberta and the railway belt of British Columbia, c. 1870-1930.\n\nLand patents contain the name of the grantee, the description of the land and the date when the land was granted. They do not contain other personal information. Homestead applications and files, which are more detailed, are held at the provincial archives.\n\n\nThe Upper Canada Land Petitions contain petitions for grants or leases of land and other administrative records. This research tool provides access to more than 82,000 references to individuals who lived in present-day Ontario between 1783 and 1865.", "owner_org": "lac-bac", "keywords_fra": "Demandes de terres,Concessions des terres,Lettres patentes,Ouest canadien,Manitoba,Saskatchewan,Alberta,Colombie-Britannique,G\u00e9n\u00e9alogie,Histoire,Terres de la Couronne"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Rapport statistique sur l'aide internationale - D\u00e9penses par pays 2011-2012", "keywords": "", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "83564003-c70c-4775-a774-ca4f070db422", "subject": "Processes  Liens et fonctions", "data_series_name_fra": "", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Annually | Annuel", "title": "Statistical Report on International Assistance - by Country Spending 2011-2012", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Ces ensembles de donn\u00e9es correspondent aux statistiques sur l'aide que verse le Canada par pays, par ann\u00e9e financi\u00e8re. Ces donn\u00e9es sont \u00e9tablies pour le Rapport statistique sur l'aide internationale que pr\u00e9sente chaque ann\u00e9e l'ACDI; elles correspondent aux donn\u00e9es de la section D du rapport, o\u00f9 les d\u00e9penses d'aide internationale sont ventil\u00e9es selon le m\u00e9canisme de prestation et le b\u00e9n\u00e9ficiaire. Puisque ces donn\u00e9es portent sur l'ensemble des d\u00e9penses d'aide internationale du Canada, elles englobent l'aide au d\u00e9veloppement officielle (ADO) vis\u00e9e par la Loi sur la responsabilit\u00e9 en mati\u00e8re d'aide au d\u00e9veloppement officielle et les autres formes d'aide officielle des divers ordres de gouvernement (gouvernements f\u00e9d\u00e9ral et provinciaux) ainsi que des administrations municipales.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "other", "url": "http://www.acdi-cida.gc.ca/INET/IMAGES.NSF/vLUImages/Open%20Data/$file/Country-Data-Stacked-2011-2012.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2013-04-30", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "", "url_fra": "", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "", "notes": "These data sets represent statistics on Canada's assistance disbursed by country, by fiscal year. This data is produced as part of CIDA's annual Statistical Report on International Assistance and corresponds to figures presented in Section D of the report, where international assistance expenditures are broken down by channel and recipient. Given that the data covers all Canadian international assistance spending, it includes both official development assistance (ODA) as per the Official Development Assistance Accountability Act and other official assistance from all levels of government (federal, provincial and municipal).", "owner_org": "cida-acdi", "keywords_fra": ""}
