{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - Aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es et proportion du territoire prot\u00e9g\u00e9 dans des pays s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9s, 2009", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,protected areas,terrestrial,marine,inland waters,international comparison,ecological area", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "7afb2937-7e7a-4aad-8527-f6ddcd1120a5", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Terrestrial protected area and proportion of land territory protected in selected countries, 2009", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur les aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es, comparaison \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle internationale indique la proportion et l'aire totale du territoire terrestre auquel diff\u00e9rents pays accordent une protection \u00e0 des fins de conservation. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n\nNote : Le graphique consid\u00e8re les zones terrestres et d'eau douce. Les r\u00e9sultats du Canada pr\u00e9sent\u00e9s ici ne proviennent que des sources de donn\u00e9es internationales. (Vous trouverez l'explication des diff\u00e9rences sous Sources des donn\u00e9es et m\u00e9thodes). Les pays s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9s sont les membres du G8, l'Australie (dont la population, la densit\u00e9 de population et la superficie s'apparentent \u00e0 celles du Canada) et la Su\u00e8de (qui pr\u00e9sente un climat similaire).", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=9DD79AE8-1#pa_5, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=22028354-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=9DD79AE8-1#pa_5, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=22028354-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/A42C78FF-A1F1-4A57-B48D-445E7B4A9034/pa_5_international_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/A42C78FF-A1F1-4A57-B48D-445E7B4A9034/pa_5_international_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2011-06-01", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The protected areas international comparison indicator reports the proportion and total terrestrial area afforded protection for conservation purposes by various countries. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n\nNote: Includes land and fresh water areas. Results for Canada are shown here using international data sources only. (Please see Data Sources and Methods  for explanation of differences.) Selected countries are the G8, Australia (the population, population density and territorial extent of which are similar to Canada's) and Sweden (which has a similar climate).", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es,\u00a0aire \u00e9cologique,terrestres,eaux int\u00e9rieures,marines,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle internationale"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des \u00e9missions de polluants atmosph\u00e9riques - \u00c9missions d'ammoniac par pays, 1999 et\u00a02009", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air pollution,international comparison,emissions,air pollutants,ammonia", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "9a5feb4d-48ff-4f26-bbdc-0504ee4dc3e4", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Pollutant Emissions Indicators - Ammonia emissions by country, 1999 and 2009", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs des \u00e9missions de polluants atmosph\u00e9riques internationaux effectuent le suivi des \u00e9missions des principaux contaminants atmosph\u00e9riques (PCA) du Canada et de neuf autres pays. Ces indicateurs aident \u00e0 renseigner les Canadiens concernant la fa\u00e7on dont les \u00e9missions du Canada se comparent \u00e0 celles d'autres pays. Les indicateurs fournissent des renseignements sur les polluants atmosph\u00e9riques principaux qui contribuent au smog et aux pluies acides et aident le gouvernement \u00e0 d\u00e9terminer les priorit\u00e9s et \u00e0 \u00e9laborer des strat\u00e9gies et des politiques pour r\u00e9duire ou contr\u00f4ler la pollution de l'air et \u00e0 effectuer un suivi des progr\u00e8s les concernant. Les donn\u00e9es sur les \u00e9missions utilis\u00e9es pour ces indicateurs servent \u00e9galement \u00e0 honorer les engagements du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale et internationale par rapport aux obligations de production de rapports. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n\nNote : Les d\u00e9finitions des sources de pollution et des m\u00e9thodes d'estimation peuvent varier d'un pays \u00e0 l'autre. Des mises en garde s'imposent lors de la comparaison des donn\u00e9es. Le produit int\u00e9rieur brut est exprim\u00e9 en million $USD constants, parit\u00e9 des pouvoirs d'achat constante, ann\u00e9e de r\u00e9f\u00e9rence 2000.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=0B0E77F5-1#nh3, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=CAA1B41D-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=0B0E77F5-1#nh3, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=CAA1B41D-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/997175CD-E34F-4B3A-A8AE-41CCE91C7C62/ae_chart4_international_nh3_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/997175CD-E34F-4B3A-A8AE-41CCE91C7C62/ae_chart4_international_nh3_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2011-11-01", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The international air pollutant emissions indicators track criteria air contaminant (CAC) emissions from Canada and 9 other countries. These indicators help to inform Canadians about how Canada's emissions compare to those from other countries. The indicators report on key air pollutants that contribute to smog and acid rain and help the government to identify priorities and track/develop progress on strategies and policies put in place to reduce or control air pollution. The emissions data used for these indicators are also used to fulfill Canada's international and domestic commitment on reporting obligations. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n\nNote: Definitions of pollution sources and estimation methods may differ from country to country. Comparisons should be made with caution. Gross domestic product values are in constant $USD, constant purchase power parities (PPP), reference year 2000, millions.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,pollution de l'air,comparaison internationale,\u00e9missions,atmosph\u00e9riques polluantes,ammoniac"}
