ource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2010-12-20", "time_period_coverage_start": "1998-01-01", "data_series_name": "National Pollutant Release Inventory (NPRI) Facility Data", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/inrp-npri/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=4A577BB9-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "1998-12-31", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/inrp-npri/default.asp?lang=En&n=4A577BB9-1", "notes": "The National Pollutant Release Inventory (NPRI) is Canada's public inventory of pollutant releases (to air, water and land), disposals and transfers for recycling. The NPRI facility pollutant release and transfer data includes:  data and information on pollutant releases, disposals and transfers for recycling that was reported by facilities in Canada and published by Environment Canada for the NPRI mandatory reporting program, under the authority of the Canadian Environmental Protection Act, 1999 (CEPA 1999).  (These pollutants include toxic substances such as the main pollutants contributing to smog, acid rain and/or poor air quality, a number of heavy metals and persistent organic pollutants.   There are important factors that should be considered prior to the use and interpretation of NPRI data and additional information is available on the NPRI web site.  NPRI data is available for the years 1993 - 2009 in a number of formats:  online query tools, downloadable databases, map layers.  In addition to the multi-year datasets, single year datasets are posted, along with corresponding database structure tables.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "polluant,pollution  \u00e9missions,environnement,recyclage,l'\u00e9limination,industrie,chimique,substance toxique,pollution de l'air,pollution de l'eau,la terre,d\u00e9versement de produits chimiques,des d\u00e9chets,injection souterraine,enfouissement,r\u00e9cup\u00e9ration d'\u00e9nergie,ozone,smog,particules,les \u00e9missions,compos\u00e9s organiques volatils,oxydes d'azote,oxydes de soufre,l'ammoniac,installations,performance environnementale,entreprises,rejets,carte,secteur"}
