{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau - Variation de l'indicateur national de la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau douce entre 2003-2005 et 2007-2009", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,national,Canadian Rivers,water quality,freshwater quality,water pollution,aquatic life,drainage region,monitoring stations", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "f3434856-3c2a-4bfb-8f28-0925a7bb3565", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Water Quality Indicators - National freshwater quality indicator change between 2003-05 and 2007-09", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur de la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau douce permet d'obtenir, gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 des stations de suivi choisies au Canada, une mesure globale de la capacit\u00e9 des plans d'eau douce de soutenir la vie aquatique. Cet outil, ax\u00e9 sur des recommandations pour la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau, est utilis\u00e9 pour synth\u00e9tiser de grandes quantit\u00e9s de donn\u00e9es sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau \u00e0 une station de suivi en un seul indice. La qualit\u00e9 de l'eau dans une station de suivi est consid\u00e9r\u00e9e comme excellente lorsque la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau ambiante ne d\u00e9passe en aucun temps les recommandations, et ce, pour tous les param\u00e8tres choisis. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=68DE8F72-1#wq2, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=5D193531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=68DE8F72-1#wq2, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=5D193531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1462CE5B-181F-4F9B-BE98-0C06715F5013/wq_chart3_change_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1462CE5B-181F-4F9B-BE98-0C06715F5013/wq_chart3_change_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-04-05", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Freshwater Quality Indicator provides an overall measure of the ability of freshwater bodies to support aquatic life at selected monitoring stations across Canada. It is a water quality guideline-driven tool used to distill large amounts of water quality data at a monitoring station into a single index. Water quality at a monitoring station is considered excellent when ambient water quality does not exceed guidelines at any time for any of all selected parameters. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale,rivi\u00e8res canadiennes,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,l'eau douce,pollution de l'eau,\u00a0vie aquatique,r\u00e9gion de drainage,stations de suivi"}
