{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des \u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre - R\u00e9partition des \u00e9missions mondiales de dioxyde de carbone dues \u00e0 la combustion de combustibles, 2009", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,greenhouse gas emissions,climate,greenhouse gases,carbon dioxide,fuel combustion,global", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "3f1c5780-73de-46b3-ba65-6ec4b4c2f441", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Greenhouse Gas Emissions Indicators - Distribution of world carbon dioxide emissions from fuel combustion, 2009", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur des \u00e9missions mondiales de dioxyde de carbone provenant de la combustion de combustibles est utilis\u00e9 pour donner une id\u00e9e de l'ampleur de ces \u00e9missions au Canada par rapport \u00e0 celles du reste du monde. L'indicateur indique la contribution du Canada aux \u00e9missions mondiales de dioxyde de carbone li\u00e9es \u00e0 la consommation d'\u00e9nergie et provenant de la combustion de combustibles en 2009 (\u00e9missions absolues), comparativement \u00e0 celles d'autres grands pays \u00e9metteurs (les pays du BRIC [Br\u00e9sil, F\u00e9d\u00e9ration de Russie, Inde et Chine], les 27 pays de l'Union europ\u00e9enne (UE-27), le Japon et les \u00c9tats-Unis) et \u00e0 celles du reste du monde. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=54C061B5-1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=CE5C9427-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=54C061B5-1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=CE5C9427-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/60A3A927-A25B-450F-A970-9A97E93EA5F4/ghg_global_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/60A3A927-A25B-450F-A970-9A97E93EA5F4/ghg_global_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-04-11", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The global carbon dioxide emissions from fuel combustion indicator is used to provide a picture of Canada's carbon dioxide emissions from fuel combustion compared with the rest of the world. The indicator reports Canada's share of global energy-related carbon dioxide emissions from fuel combustion in 2009 (absolute emissions) with those of other large emitting countries (Brazil, Russian Federation, India and China (BRIC), the 27 countries of the European Union (EU-27), Japan and the United States) compared to the rest of the world. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,\u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre,climat,gaz \u00e0 effet de serre,dioxyde de carbone,mondiales,combustion de combustibles"}
