es.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/kmz/ICDE_EA_PM10_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Air Pollutant Emissions indicators track the emissions of key air pollutants contributing to smog and acid rain in Canada. These indicators inform Canadians on the levels of air pollutants that are emitted in Canada; these pollutants can affect the air that we breathe. The air pollutant emissions indicators also help the government to identify priorities, track progress, and develop strategies and policies for reducing or controlling air pollution. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,pollution de l'air,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle locale,\u00e9missions,atmosph\u00e9riques polluantes,particules inhalables,installation"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs d'esp\u00e8ces sauvages - Changement du niveau de risque de disparition des esp\u00e8ces sauvages du Canada, 2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,wildlife,wild species,at risk,endangered,threatened,special concern,extinction,extirpation,Species At Risk Act,assessments,COSEWIC,Committee on the Status of Endangered Wildlife in Canada", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "f9df7fd4-45f0-4155-b06e-9d02a1e33a85", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Wildlife Indicators - Changes in risk of wildlife species disappearance from Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur du changement du niveau de risque de disparition des esp\u00e8ces sauvages font \u00e9tat des changements du niveau de risque de disparition des esp\u00e8ces sauvages du Canada en se basant sur les conclusions du Comit\u00e9 sur la situation des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril au Canada (COSEPAC). Le COSEPAC est un comit\u00e9 d'experts qui d\u00e9termine la situation, \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale, des esp\u00e8ces, des sous-esp\u00e8ces, des vari\u00e9t\u00e9s ou d'autres unit\u00e9s d\u00e9signables du Canada pouvant \u00eatre \u00e0 risque de dispara\u00eetre du Canada ou de la plan\u00e8te. Le COSEPAC utilise un processus incorporant les connaissance scientifiques et des collectivit\u00e9s ainsi que les connaissances traditionnelles autochtones pour \u00e9valuer les esp\u00e8ces sauvages en p\u00e9ril. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=C48CCBC7-1#wildlife_1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=39E2431F-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=C48CCBC7-1#wildlife_1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=39E2431F-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/FF180285-354D-4373-A0F6-F992CA19C0E3/cwsdr_cesi_summary_datatable_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/FF180285-354D-4373-A0F6-F992CA19C0E3/cwsdr_cesi_summary_datatable_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/FF180285-354D-4373-A0F6-F992CA19C0E3/cwsdr_cosewic_datatable_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/FF180285-354D-4373-A0F6-F992CA19C0E3/cwsdr_cosewic_datatable_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Changes in Wildlife Species Disappearance Risks indicator uses the findings of COSEWIC (Committee on the Status of Endangered Wildlife in Canada) to report on wildlife species disappearance risks in Canada. Using a process based on science and Aboriginal and community knowledge, the committee of experts determines the national status of wildlife species that are suspected of being at risk of extinction or extirpation. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,esp\u00e8ces sauvages,en p\u00e9ril,disparue,disparue du pays,en voie de disparition,menac\u00e9e,pr\u00e9occupante,Loi sur les esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril,\u00e9valuations,Comit\u00e9 sur la situation des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril au Canada,COSEPAC"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des \u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre - \u00c9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre par installation d'envergure, Canada, 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,greenhouse gas emissions,climate,greenhouse gases,carbon dioxide,carbon dioxide equivalent,large facilities", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "28e6fbf5-f9ff-4b77-8f71-c66f5b58926b", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Greenhouse Gas Emissions Indicators - Greenhouse gas emissions from large facilities, Canada, 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur des \u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre des installations d'envergure est utilis\u00e9 pour suivre l'\u00e9volution des efforts d\u00e9ploy\u00e9s par le Canada afin de faire baisser les \u00e9missions et d'atteindre les objectifs de performance environnementale. On y utilise des r\u00e9partitions par secteur et par r\u00e9gion g\u00e9ographique pour faciliter l'\u00e9laboration de politiques et de plans de r\u00e9duction des \u00e9missions. Toutes les installations qui \u00e9mettent l'\u00e9quivalent de 50 000 tonnes (50 kt) ou plus de GES (en \u00e9quivalents de dioxyde de carbone [\u00e9q. CO2]) par an doivent pr\u00e9senter un rapport \u00e0 Environnement Canada. La d\u00e9claration obligatoire des \u00e9missions par les installations donnera un tableau plus pr\u00e9cis des sources et quantit\u00e9s des \u00e9missions de GES au Canada, ce qui permettra d'\u00e9laborer, mettre en ouvre et \u00e9valuer les politiques et strat\u00e9gies du Canada en mati\u00e8re de changement climatique et d'\u00e9nergie. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=1&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=en, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=3F4A5494-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=1&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=fr, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=3F4A5494-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=1&lang=en", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=1&lang=fr", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/kmz/CESI_GHG_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/kmz/ICDE_GES_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-04-11", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The greenhouse gas emissions from large facitities indicator is used to track the progress of Canada's efforts to lower emissions and reach environmental performance objectives. Sector and geographic breakdowns are used to inform policy development and emissions reduction plans. All facilities that emit the equivalent of 50 000 tonnes (50 kt) or more of GHGs (in carbon dioxide equivalent [CO2 eq] units) per year are required to submit a report to Environment Canada. Mandatory reporting of facility emissions will provide a more precise picture of the sources and amounts of Canada's GHG emissions, thus contributing to the development, implementation and evaluation of climate change and energy policies and strategies in Canada. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,\u00e9missions de gaz \u00e0 effet de serre,climat,gaz \u00e0 effet de serre,dioxyde de carbone,en \u00e9quivalent de dioxyde de carbone,installations d'envergure"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau - La qualit\u00e9 de l'eau douce aux stations de suivi  de 2007 \u00e0 2009, au Canada", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,Canadian Rivers,water quality,freshwater quality,water pollution,aquatic life,drainage region,monitoring stations", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "00826755-9718-4285-a1d5-97cfba42626c", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Water Quality Indicators - Freshwater quality at monitoring stations for the 2007 to 2009 period, Canada", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur de la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau douce permet d'obtenir, gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 des stations de suivi choisies au Canada, une mesure globale de la capacit\u00e9 des plans d'eau douce de soutenir la vie aquatique. Cet outil, ax\u00e9 sur des recommandations pour la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau, est utilis\u00e9 pour synth\u00e9tiser de grandes quantit\u00e9s de donn\u00e9es sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau \u00e0 une station de suivi en un seul indice. La qualit\u00e9 de l'eau dans une station de suivi est consid\u00e9r\u00e9e comme excellente lorsque la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau ambiante ne d\u00e9passe en aucun temps les recommandations, et ce, pour tous les param\u00e8tres choisis. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=3&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=en, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=5D193531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=3&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=fr, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=5D193531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=3&lang=en", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=3&lang=fr", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/kmz/CESI_Water_Quality_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/kmz/ICDE_Qualite_d'Eau_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-04-05", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Freshwater Quality Indicator provides an overall measure of the ability of freshwater bodies to support aquatic life at selected monitoring stations across Canada. It is a water quality guideline-driven tool used to distill large amounts of water quality data at a monitoring station into a single index. Water quality at a monitoring station is considered excellent when ambient water quality does not exceed guidelines at any time for any of all selected parameters. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,locale,rivi\u00e8res canadiennes,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,l'eau douce,pollution de l'eau,\u00a0vie aquatique,r\u00e9gion de drainage,stations de suivi"}
