{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs d'esp\u00e8ces sauvages - Indice Liste rouge de la survie des esp\u00e8ces d'oiseaux par r\u00e9gion biog\u00e9ographique, 1988-2008", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,wildlife,bird species,global trends,Red List Index,extinction risk,ecosystems", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "c8579cd2-85dd-4e46-996f-94b2a8bd6265", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Wildlife Indicators - Red List Index of bird species survival by biogeographic realm, 1988-2008", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'Indice Liste rouge de l'indicateur sur les tendances mondiales en mati\u00e8re de survie des esp\u00e8ces d'oiseaux montre les tendances au fil du temps du risque d'extinction global (c.-\u00e0-d. am\u00e9lioration ou d\u00e9t\u00e9rioration globale du statut de la menace) des esp\u00e8ces inscrites sur la Liste rouge de l'Union internationale pour la conservation de la nature. L'indice est calcul\u00e9 \u00e0 partir de la proportion des esp\u00e8ces qui changent de cat\u00e9gorie en raison de v\u00e9ritables modifications de la situation de ces esp\u00e8ces d'une \u00e9valuation \u00e0 l'autre, et agit comme indicateur du changement de la situation de la biodiversit\u00e9 \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle mondiale. Une tendance \u00e0 la baisse de l'Indice Liste rouge indique une augmentation du niveau de risque d'extinction du groupe d'esp\u00e8ces \u00e9valu\u00e9. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=78A7AE2B-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A55B563D-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=78A7AE2B-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A55B563D-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/22BC2B76-3B05-4D02-A5C2-F1123E02EC12/RLI_datatable_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/22BC2B76-3B05-4D02-A5C2-F1123E02EC12/RLI_datatable_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Global Trends in Bird Species Survival indicator's Red List Index (RLI) shows trends over time in aggregate extinction risk (i.e., overall improvement or deterioration in threat status) over time for species on the International Union for Conservation of Nature Red List of Threatened Species. The index is derived from the proportion of species changing category due to genuine status changes from one assessment to the next, and acts as an indicator of the changing status of global biodiversity. A downward trend in the RLI indicates that the set of species assessed has moved to a higher level of extinction risk. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,esp\u00e8ces sauvages,esp\u00e8ces d'oiseaux,tendances mondiales,Indice Liste rouge,risque d'extinction,\u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs d'esp\u00e8ces sauvages - Les tendances de la taille des populations des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril par rapport aux objectifs de la strat\u00e9gie de r\u00e9tablissement, Canada, 2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,wildlife,species at risk,Species at Risk Act,recovery strategy,extripated,endangered,threatened,action plans,Committee on the Status of Endangered Wildlife in Canada,COSEWIC", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "aca22915-db90-4ff9-853d-466908ae97cd", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Wildlife Indicators - Trends in population sizes of species at risk compared to recovery strategy objectives, Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur les tendances des populations des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril fournit une \u00e9valuation des tendances en mati\u00e8re de r\u00e9tablissement des esp\u00e8ces qui rel\u00e8vent de la comp\u00e9tence d'Environnement Canada inscrites sur la Liste des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril en vertu de la Loi sur les esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril (LEP) comme disparues du pays, en voie de disparition ou menac\u00e9es, pour lesquelles il existe un programme de r\u00e9tablissement final, et dont le r\u00e9tablissement est jug\u00e9 techniquement et biologiquement faisable. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=79579EFA-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=E79097C1-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=79579EFA-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=E79097C1-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EA94E9BD-32D3-43BF-B862-18BCEB04F683/SARpop_datatable_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EA94E9BD-32D3-43BF-B862-18BCEB04F683/SARpop_datatable_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Species at Risk Population Trends indicator provides an assessment of the recovery trends of species under Environment Canada's jurisdiction that are included on the List of Wildlife Species at Risk under the Species at Risk Act (SARA) as extirpated, endangered or threatened , that have a final recovery strategy, and that are determined to be biologically and technically feasible to recover. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,esp\u00e8ces sauvages,esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril,Loi sur les esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril,strat\u00e9gie de r\u00e9tablissement,disparues du pays,en voie de disparition,menac\u00e9es,plans d'action,Comit\u00e9 sur la situation des esp\u00e8ces en p\u00e9ril au Canada,COSEPAC"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - \u00c9tat des constatations cl\u00e9s relatives \u00e0 la sant\u00e9 des \u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes du Canada", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,ecosystem,biodiversity,ecosystem health,impaired,of concern,healthy", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "82d4e3ff-9769-4eef-867c-103050bd8c55", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Status of key findings related to the health of Canada's ecosystems", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur de l'\u00e9tat des constatations cl\u00e9s relatives \u00e0 la sant\u00e9 des \u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes du Canada est \u00e9tabli en calculant le pourcentage de 20 constatations cl\u00e9s du rapport Biodiversit\u00e9 canadienne : \u00e9tat et tendances des \u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes en 2010, class\u00e9es comme \u00e9tant dans un \u00e9tat sain, pr\u00e9occupant ou alt\u00e9r\u00e9. La proportion dans laquelle ces 20 constatations cl\u00e9s s'am\u00e9liorent ou se d\u00e9t\u00e9riorent y est \u00e9galement pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e sommairement. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=28A9AD22-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=F0FFC7AF-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=28A9AD22-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=F0FFC7AF-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/7DF168E6-7572-4318-A523-E9FA279364BD/EShealth_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/7DF168E6-7572-4318-A523-E9FA279364BD/EShealth_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Status of Key Findings Related to the Health of Canada's Ecosystems indicator is based on a simple calculation of the percentage of 20 of the key findings from Canadian Biodiversity: Ecosystem Status and Trends 2010 that are rated as healthy, of concern and impaired. It also summarizes the percentage of those 20 key findings that are considered to be improving and getting worse. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,\u00e9cosyst\u00e8me,sant\u00e9 des \u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes,alt\u00e9r\u00e9es,pr\u00e9occupants,saines"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air - Niveaux ambiants de compos\u00e9s organiques volatils aux stations de surveillance, Canada, 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air quality,ambient levels,air pollutants,volatile organic compounds,concentrations,monitoring stations", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "30b0cfcd-9e67-41ec-8e80-ec037e6b43ca", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Quality Indicators - Ambient levels of volatile organic compounds at monitoring stations, Canada, 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'air pour le dioxyde de soufre, le dioxyde d'azote et les compos\u00e9s organiques volatils donnent un suivi des concentrations moyennes ambiantes de dioxyde de soufre (SO2), de dioxyde d'azote (NO2) et des compos\u00e9s organiques volatils (COV). Ces indicateurs sont con\u00e7us en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat ou de la condition afin de permettre aux analystes de politiques, aux d\u00e9cideurs et au public de d\u00e9terminer si des progr\u00e8s sont r\u00e9alis\u00e9s en vue d'une am\u00e9lioration de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air ambiant. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=20&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=en,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=20&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=fr,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?lang=en&ID=20", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?lang=fr&ID=20", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/KMZ/CESI_air_VOC_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/KMZ/ICDE_Air_VOC_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-11", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-11", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sulphur Dioxide, Nitrogen Dioxide and Volatile Organic Compounds Air Quality indicators track the average of ambient concentrations of sulphur dioxide (SO2), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and volatile organic compounds (VOC). These indicators are intended as state/condition indicators to inform policy-makers, decision-makers and the public as to whether progress is being made towards improving ambient air quality. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,qualit\u00e9 de l'air,niveaux ambiants,polluants atmosph\u00e9riques,compos\u00e9s organiques volatils,concentration,stations de surveillance"}
