{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air - Concentrations moyennes annuelles de dioxyde d'azote pour les villes canadiennes et internationales s\u00e9lectionn\u00e9es, 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air quality,ambient levels,air pollutants,international,urban areas,cities,concentrations,nitrogen dixoide", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "2703aa86-87ce-498a-b7d1-48f9eece3836", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Quality Indicators - Annual average concentrations of nitrogen dioxide for selected Canadian and international cities, 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur les comparaisons \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle internationale de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air en milieu urbain pr\u00e9sentent, pour 2010, les concentrations ambiantes d'ozone troposph\u00e9rique (O3), bas\u00e9es sur la moyenne des concentrations quotidiennes maximales sur huit heures, et les concentrations ambiantes de particules fines (P2,5), de dioxyde de soufre (SO2) et de dioxyde d'azote (NO2), fond\u00e9es sur les concentrations quotidiennes moyennes sur vingt-quatre heures. Une comparaison de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air dans les zones urbaines \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale et internationale est pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=FDBB2779-1#r4,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=E24FFEC0-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=FDBB2779-1#r4,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=E24FFEC0-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1B7C2AC9-18EA-4A27-B3B0-606CCA793281/aq_no2_international_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1B7C2AC9-18EA-4A27-B3B0-606CCA793281/aq_no2_international_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-6", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-6", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The International Comparison of Urban Air Quality indicators present, for 2010, ambient ground-level ozone (O3) concentrations based on the average of the 8-hour daily maximum concentrations, and fine particulate matter (PM2.5), ambient sulphur dioxide (SO2) and nitrogen dioxide (NO2) concentrations based on the 24-hour daily average concentrations. A comparison of air quality among Canadian and international urban areas is presented. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,qualit\u00e9 de l'air,niveaux ambiants,polluants atmosph\u00e9riques,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle internationale,zones urbaines,villes,concentration,dioxyde d'azote"}
