{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air - Concentration de compos\u00e9s organiques volatils, Colombie-Britannique, 1996 \u00e0 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air quality,ambient levels,air pollutants,volatile organic compounds,concentrations,regional", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "8eafc910-ac1d-4e60-af2a-eb3054fe4857", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Quality Indicators - Volatile organic compound concentrations, British Columbia, 1996 to 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'air pour le dioxyde de soufre, le dioxyde d'azote et les compos\u00e9s organiques volatils donnent un suivi des concentrations moyennes ambiantes de dioxyde de soufre (SO2), de dioxyde d'azote (NO2) et des compos\u00e9s organiques volatils (COV). Ces indicateurs sont con\u00e7us en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat ou de la condition afin de permettre aux analystes de politiques, aux d\u00e9cideurs et au public de d\u00e9terminer si des progr\u00e8s sont r\u00e9alis\u00e9s en vue d'une am\u00e9lioration de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air ambiant. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=95E56B3E-1#r5,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=BA9D8D27-2", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=95E56B3E-1#r5,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=BA9D8D27-2", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/575692A7-371C-4E8D-9EEB-8E6F12D6BC69/aq_voc_bc_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/575692A7-371C-4E8D-9EEB-8E6F12D6BC69/aq_voc_bc_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-2", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-2", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sulphur Dioxide, Nitrogen Dioxide and Volatile Organic Compounds Air Quality indicators track the average of ambient concentrations of sulphur dioxide (SO2), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and volatile organic compounds (VOC). These indicators are intended as state/condition indicators to inform policy-makers, decision-makers and the public as to whether progress is being made towards improving ambient air quality. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,qualit\u00e9 de l'air,niveaux ambiants,polluants atmosph\u00e9riques,compos\u00e9s organiques volatils,concentration,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle r\u00e9gionale"}
