reakdowns by jurisdiction and by ecological region are also provided. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n\nNote: Freshwater areas are included in the terrestrial area protected. The land area of Canada is 9 984 670 km2 and its marine territory is approximately 7.1 million km2. Protected areas that lack information on creation date have been allocated to a date earlier than 1990. For calculations of percentage change over time, these areas were excluded. All protected areas for which data are available are included. Overlaps between protected areas are not corrected for.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es,\u00a0\u00e9cozones,superficie prot\u00e9g\u00e9e,terrestres,marines,Grands Lacs"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - Aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es au Canada, 2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,protected areas,ecozones,parks,conservation lands,wildlife reserves,ecological reserves,migratory bird sanctuaries,ecological region,terrestrial,marine,inland waters,national,ecological area,area protected", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "27f8f3ff-c4d5-413f-9fb2-39ccfba71396", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Protected Areas in Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur les aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es indiquent la quantit\u00e9 et la proportion des aires terrestres (terres et eau douce) et marines du Canada qui ont \u00e9t\u00e9 \u00e9valu\u00e9es comme aire prot\u00e9g\u00e9e en vertu de la d\u00e9finition stipulant qu'une aire prot\u00e9g\u00e9e est \u00ab un espace g\u00e9ographiquement d\u00e9limit\u00e9, reconnu, consacr\u00e9 et g\u00e9r\u00e9, par tout moyen efficace, juridique ou autre, afin d'assurer \u00e0 long terme la conservation de la nature, avec les services \u00e9cosyst\u00e9miques et les valeurs culturelles qui lui sont associ\u00e9s \u00bb. L'acc\u00e8s aux terres et \u00e0 l'eau et leur utilisation ou les activit\u00e9s connexes sont l\u00e9galement restreints, de fa\u00e7on permanente ou temporaire, principalement dans le but de conserver la biodiversit\u00e9 et la fonction de l'\u00e9cosyst\u00e8me, ind\u00e9pendamment de la d\u00e9signation de propri\u00e9t\u00e9 (p. ex. parc, aire de conservation, r\u00e9serves de faune). Les r\u00e9partitions g\u00e9ographiques par administration et par r\u00e9gion \u00e9cologique sont \u00e9galement fournies. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n\nNote : Les aires d'eau douce sont incluses dans le total des aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es terestres. La superficie terrestre du Canada est de 9 984 670 km2 et son territoire marin est d'environ 7,1 millions de km2. Les aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es dont l'information sur la date de cr\u00e9ation \u00e9tait manquante ont \u00e9t\u00e9 allou\u00e9es \u00e0 une date ant\u00e9rieure \u00e0 1990. Ces aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es ont \u00e9t\u00e9 exclues du calcul de pourcentage de changement au fil du temps. Toutes les aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es pour lesquelles des donn\u00e9es sont disponibles sont incluses. Les chevauchements entre les aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es n'ont pas \u00e9t\u00e9 corrig\u00e9s.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/Default.aspx?id=10&Xmin=-15307263.2217053&Ymin=4878962.72110015&xmax=-5718983.26419746&ymax=11140696.5709012&lang=en, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=5FABE1CD-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?id=10&Xmin=-15307263.2217053&Ymin=4878962.72110015&xmax=-5718983.26419746&ymax=11140696.5709012&lang=fr, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=5FABE1CD-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=10&lang=en", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?ID=10&lang=fr", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-07-25", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Protected Areas indicators report the amount and proportion of Canada's terrestrial (land and freshwater) and marine area that is assessed as protected under the international definition of a protected area as \"a clearly defined geographical space, recognised, dedicated and managed, through legal or other effective means, to achieve the long-term conservation of nature with associated ecosystem services and cultural values\". Land and/or water access, use and activities are legally restricted, permanently or temporarily, primarily for the purpose of conserving biodiversity and ecosystem function, regardless of proprietary designation (e.g., park, conservation area, wildlife reserve). Geographic breakdowns by jurisdiction and by ecological region are also provided. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n\nNote: Freshwater areas are included in the terrestrial area protected. The land area of Canada is 9 984 670 km2 and its marine territory is approximately 7.1 million km2. Protected areas that lack information on creation date have been allocated to a date earlier than 1990. For calculations of percentage change over time, these areas were excluded. All protected areas for which data are available are included. Overlaps between protected areas are not corrected for.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es,\u00a0\u00e9cozones,parcs,aire \u00e9cologique,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle nationale,r\u00e9gion \u00e9cologique,terrestres,eaux int\u00e9rieures,marines,zones de conservation,refuges d'oiseaux migrateurs,r\u00e9serves fauniques,r\u00e9serves \u00e9cologiques,superficie prot\u00e9g\u00e9e"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de rejets de substances toxiques dans l'eau - Rejets de cadmium dans l'eau par source, Canada, 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,water quality,pressures on water quality,water pollution,toxic substances,cadmium,sources,releases to water,Cd", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "26daf666-bb0f-4589-92ce-ba27f55549cf", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Release of Toxic Substances to Water Indicators - Cadmium release to water by source, Canada, 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs de rejets de substances toxiques dans l'eau permettent le suivi des rejets de substances toxiques dans l'eau associ\u00e9s aux activit\u00e9s humaines au Canada. Ils contribuent \u00e0 informer les Canadiens sur les principaux polluants de l'eau r\u00e9pertori\u00e9s comme substances toxiques pour la sant\u00e9 humaine et l'environnement. Ces indicateurs aident aussi le gouvernement \u00e0 \u00e9tablir les priorit\u00e9s, \u00e0 \u00e9laborer des strat\u00e9gies et des politiques pour r\u00e9duire ou contenir la pollution de l'eau et \u00e0 v\u00e9rifier les progr\u00e8s accomplis dans ce domaine. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=7F04A6AB-1#cd2,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=3E940902-9", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=7F04A6AB-1#cd2,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=3E940902-9", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/C3A8365E-07AD-4B79-8880-84478D1E4F9F/rtsw_chart2_cd_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/C3A8365E-07AD-4B79-8880-84478D1E4F9F/rtsw_chart2_cd_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-07-26", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Release of Toxic Substances to Water indicators track toxic substances released to water by human activity in Canada. These indicators help to inform Canadians about key water pollutants that have been listed as toxic to human health and the environment. The indicators also help the government to identify priorities and to develop and track progress on strategies and policies put in place to reduce or control water pollution. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pressions sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pollution d'eau,substances toxiques,cadmium,sources,rejets dans l'eau,Cd"}
