{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air - Concentration de dioxyde d'azote, Colombie-Britannique, 1996 \u00e0 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air quality,ambient levels,air pollutants,nitrogen dioxide,concentrations,regional", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "da54fd3b-3eb9-4f36-8b7c-f6f3f4f81c31", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Quality Indicators - Nitrogen dioxide concentrations, British Columbia, 1996 to 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'air pour le dioxyde de soufre, le dioxyde d'azote et les compos\u00e9s organiques volatils donnent un suivi des concentrations moyennes ambiantes de dioxyde de soufre (SO2), de dioxyde d'azote (NO2) et des compos\u00e9s organiques volatils (COV). Ces indicateurs sont con\u00e7us en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat ou de la condition afin de permettre aux analystes de politiques, aux d\u00e9cideurs et au public de d\u00e9terminer si des progr\u00e8s sont r\u00e9alis\u00e9s en vue d'une am\u00e9lioration de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air ambiant. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=C8BFC3F2-1#r5,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=C8BFC3F2-1#r5,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/575692A7-371C-4E8D-9EEB-8E6F12D6BC69/aq_no2_bc_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/575692A7-371C-4E8D-9EEB-8E6F12D6BC69/aq_no2_bc_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-9", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-9", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sulphur Dioxide, Nitrogen Dioxide and Volatile Organic Compounds Air Quality indicators track the average of ambient concentrations of sulphur dioxide (SO2), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and volatile organic compounds (VOC). These indicators are intended as state/condition indicators to inform policy-makers, decision-makers and the public as to whether progress is being made towards improving ambient air quality. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,qualit\u00e9 de l'air,niveaux ambiants,polluants atmosph\u00e9riques,dioxyde d'azote,concentration,\u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle r\u00e9gionale"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "L'indicateur sur l'utilisation des pesticides et des engrais chimiques par les m\u00e9nages - Pourcentage des m\u00e9nages au Canada qui utilisent des pesticides et des engrais chimiques sur les pelouses et les jardins, 1994, 2005, 2007 et 2009, et par province pour 1994 et 2009", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,water quality,pressures on water quality,chemical,fertilizers,pesticides,lawns,gardens,nutrients,provinces,Canadian households", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "e1ca5745-3961-47ad-a919-7017daa00a63", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Household Use of Chemical Pesticides and Fertilizers Indicator - Percentage of households in Canada using chemical pesticides and fertilizers on lawns and gardens, 1994, 2005, 2007 and 2009, and by province for 1994 and 2009", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur l'utilisation des pesticides et des engrais chimiques par les m\u00e9nages fait \u00e9tat du pourcentage des m\u00e9nages canadiens ayant des pelouses et des jardins qui ont d\u00e9clar\u00e9 utiliser des engrais et des pesticides chimiques en 2009. Les donn\u00e9es sont divis\u00e9es par province et compar\u00e9es \u00e0 des donn\u00e9es semblables recueillies en 2005 et en 2007 concernant les engrais chimiques et en 1994 et en 2007 concernant les pesticides. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=258BC62B-1#wq_fertpest_en, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=0AAB625C-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=258BC62B-1#wq_fertpest_fr, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=0AAB625C-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/A621B230-7598-406C-919F-CCF3997A4C19/ChemicalFertilizerPesticide_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "2\tData\thttp://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/A621B230-7598-406C-919F-CCF3997A4C19/ChemicalFertilizerPesticide_en.csv\t940 B\tCSV\thttp://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/A621B230-7598-406C-919F-CCF3997A4C19/ChemicalFertilizerPesticide_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-10-04", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Household Use of Chemical Pesticides and Fertilizers reports on the percentage of Canadian households with lawns or gardens that reported using chemical fertilizer and pesticides in 2009. The data are broken down by province, and compared to similar data collected in 2005 and 2007 for chemical fertilizers and 1994 and 2007 for pesticides. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pressions sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,chimiques,pesticides,engrais,pelouse,jardins,nutriments,provinces,m\u00e9nages canadiens"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de resources biologiques - Approvisionnement en bois jug\u00e9 durable et r\u00e9colte totale, Canada, 1990 \u00e0 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,biological resources,timber harvest,wood supply,sustainable forest management,total harvest,wood volume,lumber,pulp and paper", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "866eafc6-2c60-4252-9a3a-17d2537e547f", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Biological Resources Indicators - Wood supply deemed sustainable for harvest and total harvest, Canada, 1990 to 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sustainability of Timber Harvest indicator compares the volume of timber actually harvested with the estimated national wood supply. Wood supply is the estimated volume of timber that can be harvested from an area over a specified period of time while meeting environmental, economic and social objectives. Under sustainable forest management, forest managers plan for harvest levels that will not impact the long-term sustainability of the forest resource. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=A132BB91-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A132BB91-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/6647C128-98E2-4A3D-9FEC-4B3C2BC13276/forharv_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/6647C128-98E2-4A3D-9FEC-4B3C2BC13276/forharv_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-10-04", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sustainability of Timber Harvest indicator compares the volume of timber actually harvested with the estimated national wood supply. Wood supply is the estimated volume of timber that can be harvested from an area over a specified period of time while meeting environmental, economic and social objectives. Under sustainable forest management, forest managers plan for harvest levels that will not impact the long-term sustainability of the forest resource. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,ressources biologiques,r\u00e9colte de bois d'oeuvre,approvisionnement en bois,g\u00e9rer les for\u00eats de mani\u00e8re durable,total de la r\u00e9colte,volume de bois,bois,p\u00e2tes et papiers"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Ecological integrity status and trends of 42 national parks, Canada, 2011\tIndicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - Statut et tendance de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique de 42 des parcs nationaux, Canada, 2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,national parks,ecological integrity,ecosystems,management,restoration,pressures,biodiversity,stresses", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "561bddfe-5faa-4d5f-9714-7377ae7d3ef4", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Ecological integrity status and trends of 42 national parks, Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "2012-10-04\tThe Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Park Ecological Integrity indicator reports on the ecological integrity (EI) of national parks as an indicator of the condition of Canada's protected areas. Parks Canada conducts the most complete monitoring of protected areas and is responsible for the largest proportion of any Canadian jurisdiction. This report sets a baseline for reporting future changes in ecological integrity. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\tLe programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique des parcs font \u00e9tat de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique (IE) des parcs nationaux en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat des aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es canadiennes. Parcs Canada effectue le suivi le plus complet des aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es et est responsable de la plus grande proportion d'aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es de toutes les instances canadiennes. Le pr\u00e9sent indicateur de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique des parcs sert \u00e0 \u00e9tablir un point de r\u00e9f\u00e9rence pour faire \u00e9tat sur l'\u00e9volution de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique dans le futur. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=CDE1612B-1#2", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=CDE1612B-1#2", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EADC7A74-919F-4112-BA1B-F47B6634228A/ParkEI_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EADC7A74-919F-4112-BA1B-F47B6634228A/ParkEI_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-10-04", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "2012-10-04\tThe Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Park Ecological Integrity indicator reports on the ecological integrity (EI) of national parks as an indicator of the condition of Canada's protected areas. Parks Canada conducts the most complete monitoring of protected areas and is responsible for the largest proportion of any Canadian jurisdiction. This report sets a baseline for reporting future changes in ecological integrity. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,parcs nationaux,int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique,\u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes,gestion,restauration,biodiversit\u00e9,pressions,contraintes"}
