/www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Polybrominate Diphenyl Ethers (PBDEs) in Fish and Sediment indicators are established by determining the drainage regions where concentrations are within or have exceeded the Federal Environmental Quality Guidelines (FEQGs) for PBDEs in fish and sediment. The FEQGs were developed under the Chemicals Management Plan (CMP) and are used in various ways. In this report they are used to evaluate the significance of monitoring data. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pressions sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pollution d'eau,poissons,tissus des poissons,s\u00e9diments,chimiques,PBDE,polybromodiph\u00e9nyl\u00e9thers,polluants organiques persistants,r\u00e9gions de drainage,lac Ontario,Recommandations f\u00e9d\u00e9rales pour la qualit\u00e9 de l'environnement"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - Estimation de la couverture des bior\u00e9gions par les aires marines prot\u00e9g\u00e9es (AMPs) et les sites contributifs (SCs), exprim\u00e9e en superficie totale (km2) et en pourcentage de la bior\u00e9gion (%)", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,conserved areas,marine,Great Lakes,protected areas,MPA,contributory sites,bioregions", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "f7431eb4-4236-4d6c-aa55-a482cc6e2856", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Estimated coverage of bioregions by marine protected areas (MPAs) and contributory sites (CSs), expressed in total area (km2) and as a percentage of bioregion (%)", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur les aires de conservation dans les eaux marines et les Grands Lacs pr\u00e9sentent la superficie totale et le pourcentage des oc\u00e9ans du Canada (\u00e0 partir du littoral et jusqu'\u00e0 la limite de la zone \u00e9conomique exclusive) et de la part canadienne des Grands Lacs qui sont compris dans: 1. les aires marines prot\u00e9g\u00e9es \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle f\u00e9d\u00e9rale, provinciale et territoriale; et 2. les sites contributifs, qui sont des aires de conservation qui ne r\u00e9pondent pas \u00e0 la d\u00e9finition d'une aire marine prot\u00e9g\u00e9e, mais qui ont principalement \u00e9t\u00e9 mises en place aux fins de conservation de la nature, et qui participent \u00e0 l'atteinte des buts et des objectifs du r\u00e9seau d'aires marines prot\u00e9g\u00e9es. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=0AC17F87-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=4507C531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=0AC17F87-1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=4507C531-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/C31B289D-E8FB-4889-A475-A2CA0D4A61B9/marineconservation_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/C31B289D-E8FB-4889-A475-A2CA0D4A61B9/marineconservation_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-10-04", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Conserved Areas in Marine and Great Lakes Waters indicators report the total area and percentage of Canada's oceans (from the shoreline to the limit of the exclusive economic zone) and Canada's portion of the Great Lakes that are contained within: 1. federal, provincial and territorial marine protected areas (MPAs); and 2. contributory sites, which are conservation areas that do not meet the definition of an MPA, but were established primarily for the conservation of nature and contribute to the achievement of MPA network goals and objectives. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,aires de conservation,marines,Grands Lacs,aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es,AMP,sites contributifs,bior\u00e9gion"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "L'indicateur sur la r\u00e9duction des rejets de phosphore dans le lac Simcoe - Estimation de la r\u00e9duction du phosphore \u00e0 la suite de projets de gestion b\u00e9n\u00e9ficiants du Fonds pour l'assainissement du lac Simcoe achev\u00e9s avant mars 2012", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,water quality,Lake Simcoe,regional ecosystems,phosphorus,Lake Simcoe Clean-Up Fund,recreation,drinking water,agriculture,phosphorus-reduction projects", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "b522a527-a0e7-43bf-ac77-05908f5711fd", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Reducing Phosphorus Loads to Lake Simcoe indicator summarizes estimates of the amount of phosphorus per year no longer reaching Lake Simcoe as a result of completed beneficial management projects funded by Environment Canada's Lake Simcoe Clean-Up Fund. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Reducing Phosphorus Loads to Lake Simcoe Indicator - Estimated phosphorus reduction as a result of completed Lake Simcoe Clean-Up Fund beneficial management projects completed by March 2012", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides d