 secured through the North American Waterfowl Management Plan (NAWMP) for the benefit of waterfowl. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,sauvagine,habitat prot\u00e9g\u00e9,Plan nord-am\u00e9ricain de gestion de la sauvagine,milieux humides,conservation,plans conjoints des habitats,programmes de conservation,projets de conservation"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs des habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s - Statut et tendance de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique des parcs nationaux, Canada,  2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,protected habitats,national parks,ecological integrity,ecosystems,management,restoration,pressures,biodiversity,stresses", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "f1801487-1baf-4102-9716-81547c21c158", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Protected Habitat Indicators - Ecological integrity status and trends of national parks, Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique des parcs font \u00e9tat de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique (IE) des parcs nationaux en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat des aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es canadiennes. Parcs Canada effectue le suivi le plus complet des aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es et est responsable de la plus grande proportion d'aires prot\u00e9g\u00e9es de toutes les instances canadiennes. Le pr\u00e9sent indicateur de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique des parcs sert \u00e0 \u00e9tablir un point de r\u00e9f\u00e9rence pour faire \u00e9tat sur l'\u00e9volution de l'int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique dans le futur. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=CDE1612B-1#1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=7CB5BB69-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=CDE1612B-1#1,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=7CB5BB69-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EADC7A74-919F-4112-BA1B-F47B6634228A/ParkEI_summary_en.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/EADC7A74-919F-4112-BA1B-F47B6634228A/ParkEI_summary_fr.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-10-04", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Park Ecological Integrity indicator reports on the ecological integrity (EI) of national parks as an indicator of the condition of Canada's protected areas. Parks Canada conducts the most complete monitoring of protected areas and is responsible for the largest proportion of any Canadian jurisdiction. This report sets a baseline for reporting future changes in ecological integrity. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,habitats prot\u00e9g\u00e9s,parcs nationaux,int\u00e9grit\u00e9 \u00e9cologique,\u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes,gestion,restauration,biodiversit\u00e9,pressions,contraintes"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air - Niveaux ambiants de dioxyde de soufre aux stations de surveillance, Canada, 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,air and climate,air quality,ambient levels,air pollutants,sulphur dioxide,concentrations,monitoring stations", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "dc4fcaf4-15fc-42b3-8667-069cf2579abe", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Air Quality Indicators - Ambient levels of sulphur dioxide at monitoring stations, Canada, 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. Les indicateurs sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'air pour le dioxyde de soufre, le dioxyde d'azote et les compos\u00e9s organiques volatils donnent un suivi des concentrations moyennes ambiantes de dioxyde de soufre (SO2), de dioxyde d'azote (NO2) et des compos\u00e9s organiques volatils (COV). Ces indicateurs sont con\u00e7us en tant qu'indicateurs de l'\u00e9tat ou de la condition afin de permettre aux analystes de politiques, aux d\u00e9cideurs et au public de d\u00e9terminer si des progr\u00e8s sont r\u00e9alis\u00e9s en vue d'une am\u00e9lioration de la qualit\u00e9 de l'air ambiant. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.\n", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=19&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=en,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/default.aspx?mapId=19&xMin=-17200268.28492363&yMin=4842529.641591634&xMax=-5498653.153107968&yMax=12669696.953842915&lang=fr,http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=BA9D8D27-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?lang=en&ID=19", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/TableView.aspx?lang=fr&ID=19", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/KMZ/ICDE_Air_SO2_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "kml / kmz", "url": "http://maps-cartes.ec.gc.ca/indicators-indicateurs/KMZ/Air_ICDE_SO2_n.kmz", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-06-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-9", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-9", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Sulphur Dioxide, Nitrogen Dioxide and Volatile Organic Compounds Air Quality indicators track the average of ambient concentrations of sulphur dioxide (SO2), nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and volatile organic compounds (VOC). These indicators are intended as state/condition indicators to inform policy-makers, decision-makers and the public as to whether progress is being made towards improving ambient air quality. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.\n", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,air et climat,qualit\u00e9 de l'air,niveaux ambiants,polluants atmosph\u00e9riques,dioxyde de soufre,concentration,stations de surveillance"}
