cator measures the status of major fish stocks by classifying stocks into \"healthy,\" \"cautious\" and \"critical\" categories, as outlined in the precautionary approach. This provides the fundamental piece of information required to evaluate the impacts of past fishing and to manage present and future fishing pressure. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,nature,ressources biologiques,\u00e9tat,principaux stocks de poissons,P\u00eaches et des Oc\u00e9ans,zones d'\u00e9tat des stocks,l'approche de pr\u00e9caution"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateur sur le r\u00e9tablissement des secteurs pr\u00e9occupants des Grands Lacs - Progr\u00e8s relatifs aux secteurs pr\u00e9occupants canadiens des Grands Lacs, 1987 \u00e0 2012", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,water quality,Great Lakes,regional ecosystems,restoration program,Areas of Concern,beneficial uses,Canada-United States Great Lakes Water Quality Agreement", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "9b95f467-a6a6-4160-97db-29c50287fb25", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Restoring the Great Lakes Areas of Concern Indicator - Progress on Canadian Great Lakes Areas of Concern, 1987 to 2012", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur le r\u00e9tablissement des secteurs pr\u00e9occupants des Grands Lacs fait \u00e9tat des progr\u00e8s r\u00e9alis\u00e9s vers le r\u00e9tablissement des 17 secteurs pr\u00e9occupants (SPs) canadiens en pr\u00e9sentant le nombre d'utilisations b\u00e9n\u00e9fiques cat\u00e9goris\u00e9es comme \u00e9tant \u00ab Alt\u00e9r\u00e9 \u00bb ou qui \u00ab N\u00e9cessite une \u00e9valuation plus approfondie \u00bb, de la publication du rapport d'\u00e9tape 1 au dernier rapport publi\u00e9 en 2012. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=en&n=E08EA691-1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=564BCF44-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=E08EA691-1, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=564BCF44-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1D0F33E6-C102-488F-950A-D68B4E1B7403/Great-Lakes-AOC_CSV_EN.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/1D0F33E6-C102-488F-950A-D68B4E1B7403/Great-Lakes-AOC_CSV_FR.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-12-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Restoring the Great Lakes Areas of Concern indicator assesses progress towards the restoration of the 17 Canadian Areas of Concern (AOCs) by showing the number of Beneficial Use (BU) statuses listed as \"Impaired\" or \"Requires further assessment\" from the publication of their stage 1 report to the latest report in 2012. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,Grands Lacs,\u00e9cosyst\u00e8mes r\u00e9gionaux,programme de restauration,secteurs pr\u00e9occupants,utilisations b\u00e9n\u00e9fiques,l'Accord Canada-\u00c9tats-Unis relatif \u00e0 la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau dans les Grands Lacs"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateur sur la gestion de l'immersion en mer - Sites d'immersion en mer surveill\u00e9s ne n\u00e9cessitant aucune mesure de gestion, Canada, 2001 \u00e0 2010", "keywords": "environmental indicators,water,water quality,pressures on water quality,diposal at sea,management action,ocean,excavation waste,dredging,marine pollution,disposal sites,waste,permit system", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "bdb697c2-eef2-4e6a-8651-17880ec4ab43", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Managing Disposal at Sea Indicator - Monitored disposal at sea sites requiring no management action, Canada, 2001 to 2010", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur la gestion de l'immersion en mer pr\u00e9sente les pourcentages annuels d'\u00e9v\u00e9nements de suivi qui ont d\u00e9clench\u00e9 une mesure de gestion aux sites d'immersion en mer du Canada pour les ann\u00e9es 2001 \u00e0 2010. L'indicateur fourni des renseignements permettant de d\u00e9terminer si le processus d'\u00e9valuation des permis d'Environnement Canada est en mesure d'assurer une gestion durable des sites d'immersion en mer du Canada. Les mesures de gestion sont entreprises pour assurer l'utilisation durable du site. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur est calcul\u00e9.", "digital_object_identifier": "", "presentation_form": "", "spatial": "", "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "resources": [{"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=3316493F-1#wq_das_en, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=42470330-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Dictionaire de donn\u00e9es", "language": "fra; CAN", "format": "HTML", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=3316493F-1#wq_das_fr, http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=fr&n=42470330-1", "resource_type": "doc", "name": "Data Dictionary"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/D6DB2A54-CDDB-45D9-8D4A-D90FAB139039/DaS_EN.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}, {"name_fra": "Ensemble de donn\u00e9es", "language": "eng; CAN | fra; CAN", "format": "CSV", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/D6DB2A54-CDDB-45D9-8D4A-D90FAB139039/DaS_FR.csv", "resource_type": "file", "name": "Dataset"}], "browse_graphic_url": "", "attribution": "", "topic_category": "", "attribution_fra": "", "endpoint_url_fra": "", "date_published": "2012-12-18", "time_period_coverage_start": "", "data_series_name": "Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI)", "url_fra": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=Fr&n=A073189E-1", "endpoint_url": "", "time_period_coverage_end": "", "language": "", "date_modified": "", "url": "http://www.ec.gc.ca/indicateurs-indicators/default.asp?lang=En&n=A073189E-1", "notes": "The Canadian Environmental Sustainability Indicators (CESI) program provides data and information to track Canada's performance on key environmental sustainability issues. The Managing Disposal at Sea indicator reports yearly percentages of monitoring events triggering management action for Canada's disposal at sea sites from 2001-2010. The indicator provides information about whether Environment Canada's permit assessment process is able to sustainably manage Canada's marine disposal sites. Management actions are undertaken to address the sustainability of use at the site. Information is provided to Canadians in a number of formats including: static and interactive maps, charts and graphs, HTML and CSV data tables and downloadable reports. See supplementary documentation for data sources and details on how those data were collected and how the indicator was calculated.", "owner_org": "ec", "keywords_fra": "indicateurs environnementaux,indicateur environnemental,eau,qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,pressions sur la qualit\u00e9 de l'eau,immersion en mer,mesure de gestion,oc\u00e9an,d\u00e9chets des mat\u00e9riaux excav\u00e9s,d\u00e9blais de dragage,pollution marine,site d'immersion,d\u00e9bris,syst\u00e8me de d\u00e9livrance de permis"}
{"validation_override": true, "portal_release_date": "", "data_series_issue_identification_fra": "", "catalog_type": "Data | Donn\u00e9es", "title_fra": "Indicateurs de resources biologiques - Nombre de grands stocks r\u00e9colt\u00e9s par rapport aux niveaux approuv\u00e9s, par groupe, Canada, 2011", "keywords": "environmental indicators,nature,biological resources,fish harvest,sustainable,stocks,Fisheries and Oceans Canada,harvest limits,removal reference,approved levels", "data_series_issue_identification": "", "ready_to_publish": "", "id": "ae9d32e0-db1a-410c-a93d-8c75b6a48616", "subject": "Nature and Environment  Nature et environnement", "data_series_name_fra": "Indicateurs canadiens de durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE)", "spatial_representation_type": "", "maintenance_and_update_frequency": "Unknown | Inconnu", "title": "Biological Resources Indicators - Number of major stocks harvested relative to approved levels, by group, Canada, 2011, Canada, 2011", "author_email": "open-ouvert@tbs-sct.gc.ca", "geographic_region": "", "notes_fra": "Le programme des Indicateurs canadiens de la durabilit\u00e9 de l'environnement (ICDE) rend compte de la performance du Canada \u00e0 l'\u00e9gard d'enjeux cl\u00e9s en mati\u00e8re de d\u00e9veloppement durable. L'indicateur sur les pratiques de p\u00eaches durables compare les taux de r\u00e9coltes avec les limites de r\u00e9coltes \u00e9tablies. Ces limites sont fond\u00e9es sur des informations scientifiques, ce qui nous permet de constater directement si nous g\u00e9rons l'utilisation de ces ressources \u00e0 l'int\u00e9rieur des limites de l'\u00e9cosyst\u00e8me. Cette information est rendue disponible aux Canadiens sous plusieurs formats: cartes statiques et interactives, figures et graphiques, tableaux de donn\u00e9es HTML et CSV et rapports t\u00e9l\u00e9chargeables. Voir l'autre documentation pour les sources des donn\u00e9es et pour lire comment les donn\u00e9es sont collect\u00e9es et comment l'indicateur es